"program_narrative": "Program DB2ONLN is an online (CICS) DB2 connection manager that receives a request block DB2-REQUEST-AREA from its caller (PROCEDURE DIVISION USING) and dispatches on the request type. For a connect request ('C') it checks the active-connection counter against the limit WS-MAX-CONNECTIONS (VALUE 100); below the limit it issues SQL CONNECT TO POSMVP, and on SQLCODE 0 increments the counter, returns response code 0 and builds a connection token from the current date and the counter; otherwise it returns -1 with the SQL error code and message, or the message 'Maximum connections reached'. For a disconnect request ('D') it issues SQL DISCONNECT and decrements the counter on success, or returns -1 with the SQL error details. For a status request ('S') it selects CURRENT SERVER into the error-message field and sets the response code from SQLCODE, but then unconditionally overwrites the response code with the active-connection count. Any other request type performs nothing. Every path ends with EXEC CICS RETURN. It reads no files.",
